  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "High Alert\u2019s first ability doesn\u2019t actually change any creature\u2019s power. It changes only the amount of combat damage it assigns. All other rules and effects that check power or toughness use the real values. For example, Titanic Brawl won\u2019t cause a creature to fight with its toughness under High Alert.",
      "oracle_id": "5f657279-cc0f-4431-b517-47bd1c7109b6",
      "published_at": "2019-01-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Walking Bulwark\u2019s last ability doesn\u2019t actually change any creature\u2019s power. It changes only the amount of combat damage it assigns. All other rules and effects that check power or toughness use the real values. For example, since having two creatures fight doesn\u2019t result in combat damage, an effect that causes the affected creature to fight another creature will still use its power to determine how much damage is dealt.",
      "oracle_id": "8ad0d89b-beef-40f7-8ce8-65589e3970be",
      "published_at": "2022-09-09",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Doran's ability doesn't actually change creatures' power; it changes only the value of the combat damage they assign. All other rules and effects that check power or toughness use the real values.",
